  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Comprehensive and Integrated Health Response to Emergencies in High-Priority Districts Across Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide health assistance to vulnerable communities affected by diseases. This WHO project provides the primary health care (PHC) and secondary healthcare (SHC) which will include specialized care for children, outbreaks (Dengue Fever (DF), Diphtheria, Measles, and Cholera) and MHPSS to prevent the discontinuation of essential services and increase humanitarian and life-saving access in target locations. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 263,135 people, including 65,658 women, 64,820 men, 132,657 children, and including 26,313 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
